{"availability":"available","full":"Volland/obsigraph","name":"obsigraph","description":"Typed, signed, labeled property graph for Obsidian: openCypher queries, edge properties, LadybugDB mirror, vector search, GraphRAG and MCP.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-03T09:49:05Z","updated":"2026-10-04T08:12:35Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://volland.github.io/obsigraph/","topics":["cypher","graphrag","knowledge-graph","obsidian-plugin"],"demo":"https://volland.github.io/obsigraph/demo.html","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T08:17:03.599Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T08:17:03.599Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T08:17:03.599Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T08:17:03.599Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Your Obsidian notes as a real graph: typed, signed, labeled edges with properties, openCypher queries, a graph view that shows what it means, and RAG-ready storage for agents.","Obsidian links say that two notes are related, not how. Typed Graph lets one line say how:","Then you can ask the vault questions in openCypher, inside any note:"],"features":["Typed, signed edges with properties. type:: [[Target]] {props} works like Graph Link Types, so your existing lines keep working. A - prefix makes an edge negative, and edges can have stable or pinned ids.","Typed nodes and schema notes. Frontmatter type gives a note its labels. A note in Types/ declares a type's properties, allowed edges, template and look.","openCypher queries. MATCH, OPTIONAL MATCH, WITH, aggregates, variable-length paths and path variables. Queries are read-only and errors are clear.","Graph or table, live. Results render as a labeled, styled graph or a table, and refresh as you edit.","Edge embeds. {{edge: Alice -knows-> Bob . since}} shows an edge's property inside your prose."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Volland/obsigraph/blob/main/README.m